  "title": "The Nencki-Symfonia EEG/ERP dataset",
  "description": "The Nencki-Symfonia EEG/ERP dataset contains high-density EEG recordings from healthy adults performing multiple cognitive tasks and a resting-state protocol. Tasks include an extended multi-source interference task (MSIT+), a three-stimulus oddball task, and a simple reaction task used as a control. The dataset is organized in BIDS format and supports studies of cognitive control, attention, and event-related potentials.",
  "methods_description": "EEG/ERP data were collected from healthy adult participants during four experimental conditions: (i) an extended multi-source interference task (MSIT+), (ii) a 3-stimuli oddball task, (iii) a simple reaction task (SRT), and (iv) a resting-state protocol.",
